  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/ui/src/interact.rs`: `feature_routed` also returns true while a Boundary row is armed (`state.boundary_pick.is_some()`). A viewport click then goes to `feature_click::click` and into the row. Before, with \"Click selects\" on Models, the click selected the whole model.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/do_not_touch_click.rs` (new): two tests that drive real viewport clicks into the \"Do not touch\" group of a 2D Offset.\n- `docs/decisions/3335-do-not-touch-pick.md`: the decision and the dropped options.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Reading 2 (the click route) applies to 2D Offset and 3D Pocket. These kinds show \"Pick protected\". In Models mode the click went to `pick_model`. `feature_click::ask` already took faces and edges for an armed row in every mode (#1727). Only the route did not agree.\n- Reading 1 (the kind is not supported) applies to Face, Contour, 2D Pocket, Adaptive2D, Finish3D, Trace and Engrave. This PR does not add support for them (safety floor). The sub-issues are #3343, #3344, #3345, #3346, #3347, #3348 and #3349.\n- The cause comment with the red test output is on #3335.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::tests::do_not_touch_click::do_not_touch_takes_viewport_clicks_in_models_mode`: red before the fix (`a face click adds one row: [] / selected guard`), green after.\n- `egui_app::tests::do_not_touch_click::do_not_touch_takes_a_face_and_an_edge_by_viewport_click`: green before and after. It pins the Edges-mode route: a face click and an edge click each add one row, the status line names the pick, and the remove button takes a row out.\n\n## Runs (on head 2aa9ea562)\n\n- The two pinning tests, one by one with `cargo xtask gate test ... --crate camcraft-ui --exact`: ok.\n- `camcraft-ui` lib tests: 1427 passed, 0 failed, 7 ignored.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 13 steps, 0 failed (ui build, lib and 11 ui suites).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The app was not started by hand. No screenshot: the page layout did not change.\n- The heavy lanes and the batch gate did not run. The diff is in `camcraft-ui` only.\n- The other Boundary rows (Include, Exclude, open boundary) in Models mode have no new test. They use the same route and the same `ask` rule.\n\nChangelog: Boundaries: an armed \"Do not touch\" or Boundary row now takes face and edge clicks in the viewport also when \"Click selects\" is set to Models.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3335\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
